    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In Chicago style, the approach differs from APA and does not use \"et al.\" Instead, for multiple authors, you typically cite the first few author's names followed by \"et al.\" in subsequent references. This means for your case with 5 authors, you would list all authors on your first citation, and then you would use \"et al.\" after the first author for further citations.\n\nSo in the text, your first citation would be: \"Smith, Johnson, Williams, Brown, & Wilson (2020).\"\n\nSubsequent citations would be: \"Smith et al. (2020).\"\n\nI understand that this can seem tricky when learning different citation styles. I am available to help if you have more questions or need further clarification. Best of luck with your literature review and studies!",
